    "panel_design": "494 queries with a known answer: verbatim copies of entries drawn from each arm across length bands 10-400 aa, plus the same sequences with 1-2 substitutions. Recovered = a hit whose composite fident*qcov is within 0.02 of the arithmetically expected value, which is 1.0 for a verbatim copy and (L-m)/L for m substitutions.",
    "headline": "Pooled over all 8 arms (494 query-arm pairs, each query searched against the arm that holds its answer), production defaults recover 85.4% of known prior art and the tuned length-routed settings 100%. Under 50 aa: 75.0% -> 100%. Under 20 aa: 31.0% -> 100%; at 10-14 aa defaults find 14.3% of verbatim copies and 0% of 2-substitution variants. No pair was found by defaults and missed by the tuned settings (0 of 494), 70 were found only by the tuned settings, and on the 424 pairs both settings found the tuned composite was never lower: identical on 422, higher on 2. In a further 172 of those 424 the composite was identical but a different, equally good target was cited, because PDB and SwissProt hold many identical copies of the same chain and which copy wins is arbitrary.",
    "caveats": [
      "Validated against the patent arm (uspto): 70/90 baseline, 90/90 tuned. That arm needs --split-memory-limit 3G --db-load-mode 3 and at most 4 threads on a 15 GB host, and runs 15 target splits.",
